{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams","id":1179489,"title":"How difficult do you make First Teams?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-26T05:24:47-08:00","id":1179489,"title":"How difficult do you make First Teams?","content":"So, my thoughts on this matter were, if you were to make somewhat realistic first teams prepared for garou, They'd slaughter mid rank packs more than half the time. <br /> <br /> If you'd take a former military normie, even ignoring that armour is absolute garbage according to the rules, you've got someone who'd realistically beat most garou. <br /> First, the normie would be hidden, and if the garou fail their perception check, that's an easy aimed shot. <br /> Second, the normie would very likely be well positioned/fortified as they're usually defending. The Garou would likely waste a turn getting to the individual as they move a distance, get over obstacles, or avoid traps <br /> Then, we've got between 5-7 dice, before aiming, to shoot a silver bullet from a military weapon that does between 7 and 16 base damage, the individual can split dice 2/3 times or spray. <br /> <br /> Now, this sounds very dangerous to me, multiply the threat with each individual working together tactically. You've also got possession, which could monumentally increase one's ability to fire silver and avoid claws, and you've got a couple of below average, but still trained, fools that probably only have about four dice to shoot because they were sent to die. <br /> The team has various devices at their desposal, from poison gas, to ultrasonic emiters, to claymores, and likely has silvered bayonets at the end of weapons to account for the &quot;jam weapon&quot; gift<br /> <br /> <br /> I see first teams beating fostern packs of equal size 7 times out of 10 (and first teams usually have the numbers). But I know a guy who insists they're mooks and if they use silver it'll be from a sub machinegun at worst, I leave that to regular security. So I was wondering how everyone else does them. <br /> <br /> <i>I personally don't know why anyone'd bother with a balefire thrower as the rules describe it, beyond the incredible cool factor and collateral pentex so enjoys. It's cumbersome,expensive, less effective than silver and the ammunition's a joke. </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T09:23:34-08:00","id":1179527,"title":"","content":"First teams shouldn't be easy target dummies for garou. They should force your players packs to prepare a situation, where the Team can be beaten. Maybe the first time, they will be somewhat nerved or something happens to save the pack, but from there on, whenever a First Team happens to be around, your players characters should tread carefully.<br /> Normally, I'd say not every NPC has to be perfectly equipped to deal with your PCs, but in this case, they actually are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T09:44:55-08:00","id":1179528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams#post1179489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see first teams beating fostern packs of equal size 7 times out of 10 (and first teams usually have the numbers).</div> </div> </div> </div>?? Seems like a dubious and unsourced statistic. Nothing in BotW20th suggests they are that deadly; indeed, the book seems to indicate First Team turnover is high and they die a lot, but Pentex can fill those jackets easily and it isn't a problem.<br /> <br /> You already started another thread talking about how dangerous SWAT teams should be, ect. I think you tend to overemphasize what humans are capable of, especially when fighting werewolves. Guns are all well and good but since Garou can move through the spirit world and get lots of extra actions, most humans will barely manage to pull the trigger before they are getting ripped to shreds (to say nothing of the werewolves' ability to seize the initiative via high Dex or Spirit of the Fray). Mockeries/fomorii might do a bit better thanks to their party tricks, but they aren't much of a match for Gaia's chosen either. Black Spiral Dancers are often attached to Pentex-backed raids for a reason- and that is because they have access to rage and can also step sideways.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that the Delirium is still a problem for mortals and many mockeries. There are ways that Pentex tries to mitigate it, but irrational behavior (rather than tactical thinking) is often the order of the day in a chaotic fight with Garou.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:18:08-08:00","id":1179534,"title":"","content":"High turnover among certain folk that are transfered in from accounting, sure, but dedicated team types (assault, recovery) are sourced from tried and tested teams, so win rate's gotta allow for multi-win teams. .<br /> Spirit of the frey isn;t really taken by anyone but ahrouns, and it doesn't help with the first turn from an ambush. And black spiral dancers aren't attached to first teams on pentex's request, they demand first teams, according to BoTW. Moving through the umbra isn't so much of an advantage, it takes time, you can't jump in with rage, you can't really sync it well, and they've got tools to predict entry and deny surfaces of entry.<br /> Also, at least assault rifles, silver and at least five dice to use them (to say nothing of 30. machineguns at 12, anti materials at 16 and cannons at whatever you like, then TBoTW 20th talking of how most humans go through drugs and such to improve their attributes) <i>will </i> wreck a garou's day.<br /> <br /> I want to ask you about your play experiences/scenarios you've used to reach the conclusion you have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":23728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","user":"PewPew","date":". 01-26-2018, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:30:20-08:00","id":1179537,"title":"","content":"I spent two good hours the last time, building my first team, 12 soldiers vs 4 garou (rank 2 and 3)<br /> <br /> Spirit of the fray.<br /> Just saying.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mix it with Black Spiral dancers and place all fomori instead of soldiers. It's the only way to make it <b><u>very </u></b>dangerous.<br /> Normal first teams are useful as backup troops for more powerful wyrm minions, otherwise they are really good for ambushes, just pump up their stealth rate. They can be really dangerous in this kind of situation. If the garou are going to ambush them, well, goodnight guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 01-26-2018, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:34:42-08:00","id":1179575,"title":"","content":"I think First Teams should be dangerous (they know that werewolves exist and therefore know their weaknesses), but how well they'd do against any actual pack depends on the circumstances. So while there should always be a threat that combat could go south and werewolves die, I think in most cases against PCs we'd see the PCs make decisions that will stack the deck towards them and likely victories with acceptable costs. But the threat should always be there.<br /> <br /> These kinds of combats should almost never be one on one even odds. Both sides should try to get operational advantage and strategic surprise.<br /> <br /> So First Teams when they are on &quot;routine security&quot; will be at a disadvantage since Garou will decide on when and precise places to attack. The teams will be reacting to events instead of controlling them. This is probably the most typical scenario when dealing with PCs, since it provides them the most agency.<br /> <br /> At the same time, First Teams when they go on the offensive will get all those advantages. Based on good intel, they can identify and therefore isolate individual Garou or small teams. They can choose when to attack and how. When that happens, they should have a lot of advantages since they control events and are prepared while Garou are reacting. In these cases, First Teams should be able to easily kill one or two Garou. And with enough numbers or hardware and a good plan, even wipe out small septs.<br /> <br /> I think the first scenario (teams eliminate lone or isolated Garou) to happen on an ongoing basis and is an ongoing threat and whatever frequency works out for the ST. The second scenario where small septs can be wiped out should be reserved for major plot points in a chronicle.<br /> <br /> I don't think they should be mooks. They should be a clear threat to the Garou and even PCs. But how well they do in any one situation should depend on a variety of factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T12:46:59-08:00","id":1179579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams?p=1179534#post1179534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High turnover among certain folk that are transfered in from accounting, sure, but dedicated team types (assault, recovery) are sourced from tried and tested teams, so win rate's gotta allow for multi-win teams. .<br /> Spirit of the frey isn;t really taken by anyone but ahrouns, and it doesn't help with the first turn from an ambush. And black spiral dancers aren't attached to first teams on pentex's request, they demand first teams, according to BoTW. Moving through the umbra isn't so much of an advantage, it takes time, you can't jump in with rage, you can't really sync it well, and they've got tools to predict entry and deny surfaces of entry.<br /> Also, at least assault rifles, silver and at least five dice to use them (to say nothing of 30. machineguns at 12, anti materials at 16 and cannons at whatever you like, then TBoTW 20th talking of how most humans go through drugs and such to improve their attributes) <i>will </i> wreck a garou's day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't use First Teams or Pentex in general, due to the time and setting of my own game, but the idea of well-armed, well-trained, Wyrm-aligned humans posing a serious threat to Garou is fine, on its face. But dudes with silver guns isn't 7/10 effective. To get that sort of return you have to really stack the deck against the Garou, which is what I am saying you are doing, and that isn't how any and all fights involving First Teams are necessarily set up.<br /> <br /> Related: specific weapons and tactics mean little, because things like using powerful weapons and/or your brain is something werewolves can do too. You make the assumption that the First Team is apparently smarter and better equipped than their Gaian foes. If you want to do that, fine, but there is no reason the scenario has to be constructed that way. I understand you like guns and thinking strategically, but Garou have their own weapons that hurt just as much if not more, and they have strategies and tactics of their own. Hell, they have an entire <i>dimension</i> open to them that First Teams cannot access. If you downplay the usefulness of the umbra in your own game, as you seem to, that will naturally remove a significant part of the Garou's toolkit. However, as-portrayed in setting, the hybrid nature of the Garou as half-spirit is a *massive* advantage. The Theurge in my players' pack can see both sides of the Gauntlet simultaneously, and attack across the barrier between worlds with impunity; even the lowest ranking Garou can peek to ensure they are within striking distance of a target.<br /> <br /> If you want to set up situations where very informed, insanely well armed, already-in-perfect-position First Teams blow your PC's heads off, go for it dude. But generally werewolves are portrayed as having the homefield advantage, and their senses are better than any human's. For those reasons, such a perfect ambush heavily favoring a First Team-analogue is unlikely to occur at my table (and that isn't because I run them like brain-dead mooks, I just don't understand why they should have all the odds stacked in their favor to artificially inflate the difficulty of the combat encounter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 01-26-2018, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T14:45:49-08:00","id":1179625,"title":"","content":"It should be noted that First Teams are not regular Pentex Subsidiary security. You shouldn't be seeing First Teams in many places except very secure locations or in operations where you're expecting to see professional or terrifying threats (Garou, Dies Ultimae etc). As a result what you get are First Teams as statted in the BotW20, they've got their silver knife and their clip of silver ammo, anti delirium ballistic goggle/glasses or are Fomori they may even have Pus Armour and similar tools They're well kitted, well trained and they know something of their enemy. <br /> <br /> But... They will not always, or even often, be attacking from Ambush or with complete surprise so Initiative Rolls will still play the order of the day. A lot of the contact between Garou and First Teams will be happening in tight urban conditions, engagement distances of only a few dozen feet or so, thus werewolf movement rates will cut down on the firearm advantage. Anti material Rifles are delightfully scary in theory and utterly shocking in interior urban combat, even ASRs tend to suffer which is why SMGs tend to be Armed Police weapon of choice as they handle better in tight confines. <br /> <br /> Gifts should not be overlooked (especially Jam Tech and Jam weapons) and the Umbra should really not be overlooked (on either side, where there could be First teams there are Banes). Rage and Stepping Sideways? If a pack mate is Opening/Leading The Way everyone is showing up at the same time and only the person who made the Gnosis roll isn't spending Rage that turn. Delirium is something that just isn't going to effect a First Team.<br /> <br /> Also the one real problem First Teams will have is a Garou Raging Back. Silver is great and everything but you've got to be alive after the Frenzy that follows the initial &quot;kill&quot;. Also First Teams while 'common' compared to Garou Packs are not exactly common in the World and are expensive, including replacing the fomori with limit lifespans thanks to their rather potent power boosts. <br /> <br /> First Teams are certainly a threat to a Garou Pack of pretty much any rank spread and should be handled as such. But they wont be casually eliminating packs with half a brain either, it'll be a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T15:10:11-08:00","id":1179632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams?p=1179579#post1179579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just don't understand why they should have all the odds stacked in their favor to artificially inflate the difficulty of the combat encounter).</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to war, a scenario where you can win but they'll take out most of your number is the worst kind of victory. You always want to win with minimal losses. There've been a lot of times in history where one army has really fortified a hill, and expects to defend it, and the other side just waited for the enemy to get off the hill, because the fight'd be an outright loss or a terrible victory. Hell, the battle of britain was largely won because the RAF could pick and choose which engagements to allocate resources too and what to ignore. Pentex might be evil, but they're also a business, and whilst they might vary in price from st to team, losing a first team to a stupid battle they couldn't win is a loss of an investment. <br /> <br /> Thus; Bait, Trap Kill from the Employee indoctrination book, is a really good strategy. The garou <i>need </i>to stop some polutant, so you've got land they need to take, and can fully prepare a trap/defences/plan. The garou then need to anticipate this trap/work out how to beat it, decide if the risk is worth it, or die miserably. When the garou are defending, the garou can prepare the terrain if they're even aware of a possible attack, and the FT can work out if they've got a decent attack plan or need to wait it out. Or, either side can see if going for a different target will force their opponent to move locations. Ultimately, you want to catch your opponent unawares, or make them think they'll do better than they will. Silver VS claws makes for a very quick fight, though I suspect should the FT have some kind of heavy unit to engage/distract the garou for more than a turn, they should win. Garou have more mobility, but pentex has such a resource advantage that a first team could pop up behind regular security personel and wipe out garou as they tear into poor chuck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T21:46:33-08:00","id":1179737,"title":"","content":"Dear <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23728\" data-vbnamecard=\"23728\">PewPew</a> there are one eyes and one hand about the first team issue.<br /> <br /> <b>1 Eye</b>: book sources make them look awesome and they are awesome indeed, I mean an elite human A team pumped up by some serious medicine to counter delirium along with physical or mental boost are not to be laughed at. Even a grandpa with eye cataract can knock down a crinos with a rifle shot, sincerely it happened in my games. Immagine what a team of medicine boosted pros can do. Elite a team members can easily have a wide variety of 3 dot skills and a narrow specialized set skill at 4 dots, not 5, a 5 dot skill human should be one or two in an entire continent.<br /> Their leader should be the one with greatest physical and tactical capabilities, by all means a super soldier, human not fomor (not yet), the captain america of the A team.<br /> Thus said and with the advanced arsenal both symbatic and non symbatic can kill many non combat experience packs and be a challenge even for Veteran Garou, afterall veteran Garou are the A teams of the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> <b>1 Hand</b>: In real game action A teams are slaughtered like sheep. Sincerely you make a good tactical plan and the werewolves turn it over, why? Because Garou can ambush an A team as well and can kill a full silver armed A team without a sweat, not all packs can do that and moderate stat packs can take losses, but a full combat oriented pack can decimate a full combat oriented A team because the A team makes conventional plans even though advanced ones while the PC Garou have their own variety of options that even an experienced A team leader cannot foresee. The best I have seen in my games was that an A team took down one Garou with focused full auto fire, don't expect a single shot to make the job on its own, and while they changed clips they were ripped apart, and the A team had the ambush advantage, imagine that having the advantage and it flipped around, how? Rage is the answer it can make miracles.<br /> The pack also had a special character with them who countered all the A team ambush, well the A team didn't expect that...... and even medicine have duration and expire.<br /> <br /> Then you hear only screams, screams and thundering growls that blanket the booming of the bullets.<br /> -Johnson, Johnson! A pack, repeat! A pack, answe me!<br /> From behind: Gwrrrrr<br /> -Oh my Go..... pshshshsh...<br /> Silence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 01-27-2018, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T06:05:49-08:00","id":1179803,"title":"","content":"First Teams (IMHO) cannot get even returns from combat with Garou. Even the heavy combat fomori are not an even match one-for-one. For the humans (or mostly-humans) it's really no contest... But... That's not really the point. Even if they lose a hundred of their people for every Garou they bag, that's a win. The First Teams' single greatest advantage is their ability to win through simple attrition. EVERY Garou that falls is irreplaceable. Every hundred First Team troops that fall have another hundred to replace them. Pentex is simply that vast. They're NOT mooks... They're the consequence of the Garou turning the humans into enemies. For all of their power, the Garou are simply not equipped to deal with the human birth rate, and the best they can hope for from Humanity in the modern age is for them to remain largely ignorant to the Garou's very existence. The First Teams are a dark reminder of the fate that lies in store for the Garou Nation should the Veil ever be irreparably torn: An enemy armed to the teeth with the most advanced technology that humankind can craft, silver, and a human's intellect -- in almost unfathomable numbers.<br /> <br /> \u200bHow tough should they be? However tough it takes to make the pack really work for their victory... and if the players get arrogant or too confident of that victory (like thinking of the First Teams as nothing more than &quot;mooks&quot;) -- <i>just</i> tougher than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T07:08:26-08:00","id":1179821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams?p=1179803#post1179803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even the heavy combat fomori are not an even match one-for-one.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Not on average. But I have seen a decked out to the gills, super powerful fomor defeat a Garou 1 on 1. It happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-27T15:53:11-08:00","id":1179960,"title":"","content":"I break my first teams into four groups: Alpha Teams, who are the elite best of the best; Beta Teams, who are average trained combatants; Gamma Teams, who are cannon fodder mooks; and Omega Teams, who are suicide squads (usually made up of fomori on their last legs, people with terminal diseases, the mentally unstable, and the like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T02:53:27-08:00","id":1180108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams?p=1179821#post1179821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True. Not on average. But I have seen a decked out to the gills, super powerful fomor defeat a Garou 1 on 1. It happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Partially blind grandpas with rifles too, man I am not joking, grandpas and rabbits can turn a garou's day really bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T08:15:38-08:00","id":1180168,"title":"","content":"As a note about also First Teams hiding really well, and having all the strength in an ambush, the W20 core plays up how strong a Garou's senses are on page 273. It mentions that the Garou tend to use their senses instinctively, and points out that even in homid form, Primal Urge can be used to pick up things like hidden threats. The table shows that a &quot;well-concealed prey, enemy, trail, or item&quot; is only a diff 6. If the First Team gets access to something magical for hiding it raises the diff to an 8....higher sure but not unimaginable. Hiding isn't a guaranteed ambush....I've tried to do the whole First-Team ambush thing, and had my players find them before the First Team was going to strike. Sure as a GM you could rule they have to say &quot;I am looking out for threats&quot; and therefore you can hope you catch you PC's by hitting them when its not demanded. For me, the fact that your senses can pick things up instinctively, means that they PC's should at least get their Primal Urge rolls however as a chance to know about the ambush before it happens (I also don't like the idea of &quot;it rains silver, you die&quot;).<br /> <br /> Side note...30 dice of damage for some of the weapons....what weapon/book is this coming from? Are you relying on getting all successes from a auto fire with a 5 dex and 5 fire arm? Because while possible....with the enhanced diff from full-auto rather unlikely....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 01-28-2018, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:10:24-08:00","id":1180482,"title":"","content":"oh curious, how should a subaltern pack fare against a first team? <br /> <br /> since Subaltern packs dont have to worry about silver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T13:21:39-08:00","id":1180489,"title":"","content":"What is a Subaltern pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T15:21:55-08:00","id":1180518,"title":"","content":"a group of kinfolk who work together in imitation of a garou pack, also called a plebe pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T17:30:42-08:00","id":1180550,"title":"","content":"So...instead of worrying about silver bullets, they have to worry about bullets?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T19:27:52-08:00","id":1180576,"title":"","content":"It's pretty much an even playing field at that point. A combat focused subaltern pack probably relies on the same sorts of military equipment and tactics as a First Team, with whatever supernatural edges they can get. And all human First Team and all normal Kinfolk subaltern pack is going to be like two military fireteams going at it. First Teams can have fomori, but Kin might have Numina, be Kami, or have Gifts to balance that out. First Teams might get some special tech, Kin might get some talens or even a Fetish that's Kin-usable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T02:53:38-08:00","id":1180654,"title":"","content":"I'd say PFT would beat an equally sized kinfolk pack. Kinfolk are very unlikely to have gifts/numina or be kami, and unless they're with glass walkers they're going to have inferior gear and weaker training.(if they are with glass walkers, prepare for anything between advanced materials to iteration X) Of course, they'll be more stable and careful without formori, but I think they'll fare terribly should one of them be more than easy to deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T09:18:15-08:00","id":1180755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams?p=1180654#post1180654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say PFT would beat an equally sized kinfolk pack. Kinfolk are very unlikely to have gifts/numina or be kami, and unless they're with glass walkers they're going to have inferior gear and weaker training.(if they are with glass walkers, prepare for anything between advanced materials to iteration X) Of course, they'll be more stable and careful without formori, but I think they'll fare terribly should one of them be more than easy to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the kinfolk have fetishes their weapons may be superior to the first team. And the 'likelihood' of having gifts or being Kami is really neither here nor there. There is nothing that says a given scenario in WtA must be populated by the most common or typical members of any given group or tribe. None of this is real. If I am a storyteller, creating the scenario, I can do whatever I want to level the playing field and there are lots of reasons I could come up with to do so. 'First team guns down bunch of ill-equipped kinfolk' isn't terribly compelling or interesting stuff in the first place; it still seems like you are laboring under the impression that 'guns and a modicum of spec-ops training = win.' In fantasy land with spirit powers and shapeshifting, this is hardly a given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T10:33:46-08:00","id":1180800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PewPew</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1179489-how-difficult-do-you-make-first-teams?p=1180654#post1180654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say PFT would beat an equally sized kinfolk pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on what? There is nothing inherent in &quot;First Team&quot; that gives an advantage that kinfolk can't get. They might beat an &quot;average&quot; group of kinfolk, but that's because there's a lot more kin than First Team members and most kin aren't in combat unit packs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kinfolk are very unlikely to have gifts/numina or be kami, and unless they're with glass walkers they're going to have inferior gear and weaker training.(if they are with glass walkers, prepare for anything between advanced materials to iteration X) Of course, they'll be more stable and careful without formori, but I think they'll fare terribly should one of them be more than easy to deal with. </div> </div> </div>Kinfolk with access to combat focused Gifts, Numina, or are Kami with relevant Powers, are way more likely to be recruited for such things. You're also going against established things here. The Glasswalkers aren't the only option here. The Black Eagles are a primarily Get kin organization of special forces level mercs with access to all sorts of military grade gear; on top of any overtly magical gear they might take as payment from Garou that employ them but aren't rolling in cash.<br /> <br /> Then there's issues like home-field advantage. First Teams are sent where Pentex wants them. Most combat oriented kin packs are locals fighting locally. The last century of international conflict has demonstrated time and time again that &quot;better trained and better equipped foreigners,&quot; loses to, &quot;locals that know what the fuck they're doing even with outdated equipment.&quot; I wouldn't give a First Team decent odds against a purely human Somali militia if the militia is fighting on its home turf, let alone a militia that's actually controlled by a Gnawer and Strider kin pack that took the militia over by force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}